course: dictionary
lesson: 14377
title: The ordinate: how high is the point?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: On a graph, every point has two numbers in brackets, like (3, 5). The first number tells you how far across the point is. The second number tells you how far up or down it is. «The point (3, 5) has the ordinate 5.»
explain: The ordinate is the second number: how far up or down the point is from the x-axis, the flat line across the bottom of the graph. If the ordinate is negative, the point is below the x-axis.
explain: The first number is called the x-coordinate, or abscissa. In everyday school maths, people mostly say "y-coordinate" for the ordinate. «Find the y-coordinate of the point (2, 6).» Here it means the same as ordinate.
fact: The ordinate is a point's height on a graph, also called its y-coordinate.
fact: In the point (3, 5), the ordinate is 5 and the x-coordinate is 3.
fact: «Ordinate» means how far up or down a point is from the x-axis.
fact: The x-coordinate is also called the abscissa.
fact: Schools mostly say "y-coordinate", so when you hear ordinate, think "the second number in the brackets".
exercise: «In the point (4, 7), what is the ordinate?» | 11 | 4 | *7 | 3
exercise: «The point (2, 6) is plotted on a graph. Which number is its ordinate?» | 8 | The point is on the x-axis | *6 | 2
exercise: «Find the ordinate of the point (5, 1).» | 6 | 0 | *1 | 5
test: «The point (8, 3) is 3 units up from the x-axis. What is its ordinate?» | 5 | 11 | 8 | *3
test: «Which number tells you how far up the point (1, 9) is?» | 10 | It is not a number | *9 | 1
exam: «The ordinate of point P is 9, so P is 9 units above the x-axis.» What does ordinate mean? | How far across a point is from the y-axis | A line that goes through the middle of a graph | *How far up or down a point is from the x-axis | The number of points on a graph
